/T (Meta Title and Meta Description are HTML elements that provide a brief summary of a webpage for both search engines and users. The meta title appears as the clickable headline in search results, while the meta description appears below it as a short overview of the page. Together, they help search engines understand the page's content, improve visibility in search results, and encourage users to click on the webpage.)
